    Since round 8 of MESHSAT-1357 (26 September 2026): the controller reads `EMCON_HW` only through `U13`, a second 74LVC1G17, and `R46` (1k) on GPIO 21, so no firmware pin sits on the line (`feasibility/EMCON.md` item L1); and the hardware EMCON lamp of SD-EMC-6 is drawn: `U14`, a TI SN74LVC1G57 wired as a NOR with Schmitt inputs, reads `TX_INHIBIT_n` and `EMCON_HW` and turns on `Q7` (Si2300DS), which sinks `D22` from `LED_RAIL_SW` through `R47` (470R), so the lamp is lit only while both lines read LOW, with no processor in its path.
