V2-SPEC.md#Thermal and environment:L73:para:s1 [286e14a698] TRUE
    no vent opening anywhere in the case skin or the plate (owner ruling 7 Sep 2026, 32.53): the heat leaves through the aluminium face plate and the case walls; five IP68-rated internal fans (one per CM5 cooler, driven by its module, and two mixer fans under the plate, driven by the sensor controller; correction 32) couple the inside air to the skin; the 30 W PA module bolts flat to the plate's underside on two PEM nuts with a thermal pad (32.56); estimated inside-air rise about 10 K with one module and 16 K with three loaded modules with the lid open (32.53), to be measured by `TEST-PLAN.md` E3; the kit is to be operated shaded, a stated operating condition, with a shade accessory (a lid sun shield or a tarp) and full-sun design a later qualification item (owner ruling D-02e, 26 Sep 2026); with the lid closed the kit runs the reduced mode (owner ruling D-02b of 25 Sep 2026: closed-lid operation in a defined reduced mode, for example GNSS, LoRa mesh, Iridium and APRS beacons, monitor off and one module, with a closed-lid state and thermal test to join `TEST-PLAN.md` and a lid sensor, drawn on board E since `faf8c981` (correction 19); accepted consequences: above +35 C ambient the kit runs one module, and with three loaded modules charging holds off above about +25 C ambient); both restrictions are proposed controls, not established limits: with the current heat budget the design record's own conductance puts the charge hold-off for three typical modules at +19.5 to +21.6 C, the independent bound anywhere from -18 to +19 C, and the hot end is undecided until the enclosure conductance is measured; the design implements the restrictions as controls on the measured pack current and temperatures (the thermal controls C1 to C4 of `feasibility/POWER-THERMAL.md` section 9.3, not the case choices of line 9; the session's choice), and an early heat-balance test is proposed there (finding PWR-F08, feasibility blocker FEA-004; correction 23); the pack's heater mat and the inside climate sensor set the cold-weather behaviour, and a start from a pack cold-soaked below about -10 C at the cells is out of scope for the prototype: it needs shore or vehicle power, or warming, first (owner ruling D-02d, 26 Sep 2026); the case keeps Peli's own pressure equalisation valve (correction 10).
    judgement: the fans: the coolers on their modules, the mixers on E's sensor controller; the thermal text is the record's
    names looked up: 2 parts, 0 nets
    asserted (13): B J_FAN1.4 on FAN_PWM1 (netlist: FAN_PWM1); B U30A Fan_PWM on FAN_PWM1 (netlist: FAN_PWM1); B J_FAN1.3 on FAN_TACHO1 (netlist: FAN_TACHO1); B J_FAN2 present; B J_FAN3 present; E J_FAN1.3 on FAN1_TACH (netlist: FAN1_TACH); E U10.13 on FAN1_TACH (netlist: FAN1_TACH); E U10 value has 'RP2040' (netlist: 'RP2040 sensor controller (USB to B16 through the dock)'); E Q9.3 on FAN1_SW (netlist: FAN1_SW); E J_FAN1.2 on FAN1_SW (netlist: FAN1_SW); E J_FAN2 present; board E: 2 parts whose designator holds 'J_FAN' (read: 2, J_FAN1,J_FAN2); board B: 3 parts whose designator holds 'J_FAN' (read: 3, J_FAN1,J_FAN2,J_FAN3)
